---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="mdbase Connect"
  description="Host, share, and synchronize Markdown collections, serve local folders to applications, and control access through explicit permissions."
  current="connect"
>
  <section class="content-section" aria-label="About mdbase Connect">
    <h1 class="sr-only">mdbase Connect</h1>
    <p>
      mdbase Connect makes Markdown collections available to applications. It
      hosts collections online, lets you share them with other people,
      synchronizes them with local copies, and manages application access.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a collection is hosted, Connect serves its online copy directly.
      When a collection remains on your computer, the mdbase Connector serves
      the folder locally. Connect still manages approval, but the contents of
      local operations do not pass through the hosted service.
    </p>
    <p>
      When an application asks for access, you choose a collection and review
      what it needs to do. The permission applies only to that application and
      collection and can be narrowed, paused, or revoked later.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="share-a-collection">
    <h2 id="share-a-collection">Share a collection</h2>
    <p>
      Owners can invite other people to a hosted collection as viewers or
      editors. Viewers can read; editors can read and change records but cannot
      manage membership. Each member’s applications and mirrors stay within
      that member’s permissions. Owners can change roles or remove access later.
    </p>
    <p>
      To share a collection, open its sharing controls in the <a href="https://editor.mdbase.dev/">mdbase Editor</a> and invite someone
      by email. The recipient must already have a registered, verified Connect
      account. After accepting, they can open the collection in compatible
      applications; applications requiring permissions beyond their role cannot
      be connected.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sharing applies to hosted collections, not local folders served by the
      Connector. It provides access to the same records, not simultaneous live
      co-editing of a note.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can <a href="/downloads/">download the Connector</a> to use local
      folders, <a href="/beta/">create a Connect account</a> for hosted
      collections, or <a href="https://connect.mdbase.dev/login">sign in</a> to
      manage an existing account.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
